Net income (loss) attributable to The AES Corporation

    Net loss attributable to The AES Corporation increased $137 million, or 33%, to $546 million in 2022, compared to $409 million in 2021.
This increase was primarily due to:

     •   Higher goodwill impairments in the current year;

     •   Prior year gain due to the initial public offering of Fluence;

     •   Higher income tax expense;

     •   Prior year gain on remeasurement of our equity interest in the sPower development platform to acquisition date fair value;

     •   Higher Parent interest expense due to prior year realized gains on de-designated interest rate swaps, higher interest rates, and higher
        outstanding debt;

     •   Lower margins at our US and Utilities SBU due to the recognition of previously deferred power purchase costs, impacts of outages, and
        unrealized derivative losses;

     •   Lower capitalized interest at construction projects in Chile; and

     •   Other-than-temporary impairment of sPower.

